# Commands that may appear in <src>/.cadinstall.post-exec.sh.
# A script line must be exactly one of these commands, then its arguments,
# then one relative path under ./. The installer only knows how to safely
# parse chown, chmod, and chgrp; any other entry here is a configuration error.
#
# Optional flag: -R
# chown operand: <user> or <user>:<group>
# chmod operand: 3 or 4 octal digits
# chgrp operand: <group>
# Path: ./ (the release itself), ./relative/path, or a glob such as ./*
# A path containing .. is rejected. ./* cannot climb out of the release.
sudo /usr/bin/chown
sudo /usr/bin/chmod
sudo /usr/bin/chgrp
